  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Financing Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Global Health (GH)):  The GFF contribution will enhance country and global efforts to create resilient, epidemic-ready, and sustainably financed primary health care systems and health workforces that are capable of responding during health emergencies arising from emerging infectious disease threats. COVID-19, Ebola, and other major outbreaks have illustrated that infectious disease threats can overwhelm fragile primary health care systems and disrupt routine prevention and treatment services with disastrous implications. Strong primary health care systems are also the prerequisite for establishing the community-based surveillance needed to detect new infectious disease threats, delivering rapid frontline responses, and providing outbreak and pandemic response services throughout the duration of the health emergency. This funding, through a direct agreement with the World Bank, will provide technical assistance to governments to strengthen resilient, epidemic-ready primary health care systems that are capable of effectively delivering outbreak and pandemic response services. It will strengthen the ability of governments to support routine health information systems and rapid assessments to track disruptions in services due to pandemics or other emerging health threats, and more rapidly respond based on near-real-time signals.</narrative>
  </description>
